	abstract = {In current society, plagiarism of material from external sources is common and claiming it as one's own is considered a serious offense, particularly in academic settings. Plagiarism has become a significant issue among students at all levels-undergraduate, postgraduate and even doctoral. This paper addresses the specific challenge of plagiarism in computer programming assignments, where students frequently blend and modify original solutions to produce fraudulent work. To address this issue, a system has been proposed that enables teachers to efficiently check for plagiarism with a single click by uploading a folder of submissions. Although various software tools have been developed to detect plagiarism, there has been limited evaluation of their effectiveness in accurately identifying the true authorship of submitted work. Our approach leverages artificial intelligence algorithms to break down submitted articles into smaller sections and compare them against existing databases. This research aims to effectively identify and recognize instances of plagiarism while preventing potential copyright issues. Index Terms - Plagiarism detection, Text similarity, Machine learning, Cosine similarity, Semantic analysis  © 2025 IEEE.},
